  "more_sources": "Data sources",
  "more_sourcesBody": "• IOC Sea Level Monitoring — measured sea level at Vung Tau and Quy Nhon (every minute). Tide forecasts at these 2 stations are computed by harmonic analysis (utide) from 12 months of data; backtest error: ±10 cm (Vung Tau), ±7 cm (Quy Nhon).\n• National Center for Hydro-Meteorological Forecasting (KTTV) — short-range hydrological bulletins: river levels 4 times/day + forecast. Hourly lines are estimated by the app (combined with estuary tide); backtest: ±12 cm (Hanoi), ±11 cm (Nam Dan).\n• Open-Meteo — weather, waves and coastal sea level model.\n• GloFAS (via Open-Meteo Flood) — daily main-channel river flow.\n• Any point on the map: ocean model at that point; on the Red River and Ca River, calculated from position along the river; elsewhere uses the nearest KTTV river station (within 40 km), coastal tide (estimated) or river flow.\n• Base map: OpenFreeMap · © OpenMapTiles · data © OpenStreetMap.\n• Satellite imagery: EOxCloudless (EOX IT Services GmbH), contains Copernicus Sentinel 2025 data.\nAll forecast/estimated figures are for reference only. See each station's Info tab for source details, datum and reliability.",
