  "knot_note": "General tips: wet the knot before tightening, pull slowly so it does not heat up, trim leaving 2–3 mm. Drawings are diagrams.",
  "knot_improvedClinch": "Improved clinch knot",
  "knot_improvedClinch_use": "Hooks and snaps on mono. The easiest one; everyone should know it.",
  "knot_improvedClinch_steps": "Pass the line through the hook eye, leaving about 15 cm.\nWrap the tag end around the main line 5–7 times.\nPass the tag through the small loop by the eye, then through the big loop you just made.\nWet it, pull the main line tight, trim.",
  "knot_palomar": "Palomar knot",
  "knot_palomar_use": "Hooks and lures on braid (PE). Very strong and quick.",
  "knot_palomar_steps": "Double about 15 cm of line and push the fold through the hook eye.\nTie a loose overhand knot with the doubled line.\nPass the whole hook through the folded loop.\nWet it, pull both ends tight, trim.",
  "knot_uni": "Uni knot",
  "knot_uni_use": "Hooks, snaps and lures; works on mono and braid.",
  "knot_uni_steps": "Pass the line through the eye and lay the tag alongside the main line to form a loop.\nWrap the tag around both lines inside the loop 5–6 times.\nPull the tag so the wraps sit neatly.\nWet it, pull the main line to slide the knot to the eye, trim.",
  "knot_doubleUni": "Double uni knot",
  "knot_doubleUni_use": "Joins two lines (braid to mono leader, or a broken line).",
  "knot_doubleUni_steps": "Overlap the two line ends by about 20 cm.\nWith the first end tie a uni knot around the second line (3–4 wraps; 6–8 for braid).\nDo the same with the second end.\nWet them, pull the main lines so the knots slide together, trim.",
  "knot_perfectionLoop": "Perfection loop",
  "knot_perfectionLoop_use": "A loop at the line end to clip rigs and leaders on fast.",
  "knot_perfectionLoop_steps": "Make a small loop at the end, tag behind.\nWrap the tag around to make a second loop in front.\nPass the tag between the two loops.\nPull the second loop through the first, tighten, trim.",
  "knot_snell": "Snell knot",
  "knot_snell_use": "Ties a hook so the line runs straight down the shank, hooking more fish.",
  "knot_snell_steps": "Pass the line through the eye and lay it along the shank to make a loop.\nWrap the loop around the shank and line 7–8 times, from the eye down.\nHold the wraps and pull the main line tight.\nWet it, tighten again, trim.",
